OL,3,GNEWSAOne of Scotland's last D-Day
OL,4,Aveterans dies, aged 100
OL,5,
OL,6,FOne of Scotland's last surviving D-Day
OL,7,Fveterans, who helped clear sea mines
OL,8,Foff Omaha Beach during the Normandy
OL,9,Flandings, has died aged 100.
OL,11,FCharlie Horne was 18 years old when he
OL,12,Fserved on a small wooden minesweeper
OL,13,Fwhich came under fire on 6 June 1944.
OL,15,FThe former trawlerman from Prestonpans
OL,16,Fin East Lothian said the scenes of
OL,17,Fdevastation he witnessed as Allied
OL,18,Fforces landed in France stayed with him
OL,19,Ffor the rest of his life.
